{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>When Israel went out</b> — a lo'ez from the words of our Rabbis of blessed memory, like the expression 'a foreigner's tongue upon her sons' or regarding foreign languages."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 114, :notes {0 "The Hebrew here is itself a wordplay: Ibn Ezra is explaining the term לועז as derived from rabbinic usage, likely alluding to a phrase whose exact source is uncertain; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:35.986014710Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}